🟡 Q1 — Update one column

Increase Himani's salary to 60000.
UPDATE employees
SET salary=60000
WHERE employee_name='Himani';

🟡 Q2 — Update multiple columns

UPDATE employees
SET department='Data Science',salary=55000
WHERE employee_id=2;

Do it in one UPDATE statement.

🟡 Q3 — Update using a condition

Increase the salary of everyone in Data Science by 5000.
UPDATE employees
SET salary=salary+5000
WHERE department='Data Science';

🟠 Q4 — Delete using a condition

Delete employees whose salary is less than 45000.
DELETE FROM employees
WHERE salary<45000;

🟠 Q5 — Delete by department

Delete everyone from the Electronics department.
DELETE FROM employees
WHERE department= 'Electronics'; 

🔴 Q6 — Challenge

Increase the salary by 10% for employees whose current salary is at least 50000.

UPDATE employees
SET salary=salary*1.10
WHERE salary>=50000;

💡 You don't need to calculate each salary manually.
